# The stylesheet of the development instances, on every page.
#
# The academic extensions ship no stylesheet of their own. Their markup is
# styled by the site package, and this is that part of the development
# instances: one file compiled from "Resources/Private/Scss/frontend/" of this
# package, with a shared partial and one per extension. An installation copies
# what it needs into its own site package.
#
# Included by the static template of this package for the "/legacy/" tree, and by
# the set "fgtclb/academics-dev-site-stylesheet" for the "/" tree, where it comes
# after the stylesheets of the theme.
#
# The interface stylesheet of CKEditor 5 comes first, and only on a page with the
# profile editor of EXT:academic_persons_edit. The editor imports CKEditor 5 from
# the import map of EXT:rte_ckeditor, and from TYPO3 13.4.36 and 14.3.8 on the
# styles of its toolbar, buttons and balloons are no longer injected by its
# scripts. They are in "editor.css" of EXT:rte_ckeditor, which the backend form
# links and a frontend page does not. Linking the file of the core keeps the
# styles at the version of the editor the core ships. Before those patch levels
# the file holds a few TYPO3 additions only and the scripts bring the rest.
page.includeCSS.academicsDevSiteRichTextEditor = EXT:rte_ckeditor/Resources/Public/Css/editor.css
page.includeCSS.academicsDevSiteRichTextEditor.if.isTrue.numRows {
    table = tt_content
    select.where = {#CType} = 'academicpersonsedit_profileediting'
}
page.includeCSS.academicsDevSite = EXT:academics_dev_site/Resources/Public/Css/frontend/academic-extensions.css
